{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789897452,"nonce":"yyO2iMpMdcHFdFny3o1ncNDdL1s=","title":"Lua: numeric for with a float limit, a large step or a literal zero step","message":"A float limit of an integer loop was floored whatever the step, so for i = 1, 0.99999, -1 ran twice; one past the integers on the side the step moves away from clamped to the range's end and ran once from that end. The loop left at the limit itself, which a step larger than one can carry past into a wrap: for i = mini, maxi, maxi ran on after maxi - 1. A literal zero step raised nothing and, in a float loop, spun forever.","files":null}]}